\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I hoped that with the brave and strong
\par My portioned task might lie;
\par To toil amid the busy throng,
\par With purpose pure and high:
\par But God has fixed another part,
\par And He has fixed it well;
\par I said so with my breaking heart,
\par When first this trouble fell.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. These weary hours will not be lost,
\par These days of misery,
\par These nights of darkness, tempest-tossed,
\par Can I but turn to Thee,
\par With secret labour to sustain
\par In patience every blow,
\par To gather fortitude from pain,
\par And holiness from woe.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. If Thou shouldst bring me back to life,
\par More humble I should be,
\par More wise, more strengthened for the strife,
\par More apt to lean on Thee;
\par Should death be standing at the gate,
\par Thus should I keep my vow:
\par But, Lord, whatever be my fate,
\par O let me serve Thee now!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

